// meta-bl.js — Meta Deep Dive ▸ Bottom Line ▸ General (BL-GEN-1…5, docs/PROFILE_PLAYBOOK.md §13).
//
// COPIED from js/overviews/tsm-bl.js (itself the dependency closure of amzn.js's aMarginsBody · aBridgeBody ·
// aNetBridgeBody · expenseTabsBody · aBlFootGeneral · aBuildMargins · aBuildExpenses), plus amzn.js's aSbcBody /
// aBuildSbc, then adapted to Meta — never reimplemented:
//   • data: ./meta-bbg.js (Bloomberg export, generated by scripts/bbg_extract.py) for the income statement and
//     consensus; ./meta-bl-data.js for the reported functional expense lines (10-K / 10-Q via SEC XBRL), SBC by line,
//     the one-time tax items and the expense-line dives; ../results-data/meta.js for the quarterly operating-income
//     series and the Summit series.
//   • expense lines = Meta's own (10-K MD&A): cost of revenue · research and development · marketing and sales ·
//     general and administrative. Meta has no "other operating" line — the four tie to income from operations.
//   • cost of revenue goes FIRST and apart in every bridge view, with a Gross profit subtotal (§13, SAB 2026-10-19),
//     and the bridge has the fourth mode "Cost structure" (stacked % of revenue over time).
//   • Normalized net income = GAAP + the 3Q25 OBBBA deferred-tax charge, − the 1Q26 CAMT-relief benefit (both from
//     the filings, META_TAX_ONEOFF) — Meta's distortion is a tax item, not an investment mark, so Amazon's
//     "strip the non-operating gain" rule is replaced by these two items.
//   • Summit series: read from js/results-data/meta.js, where the Summit DCF model is FROZEN (rule 10 — coded from the
//     dated snapshots, not live). Every Summit chip says "frozen"; the footer names the snapshots, read off the data.
//   • Annex A fixed in the copy: no typed years or labels (A12); shares axis on the RIGHT (A9); no inline <style>
//     (A1/A10; styles in css/overview.css under :is(.ov-tsm-dd, .ov-meta-dd)); no hex colours (Summit tokens from
//     js/viz-palette.js); DOM lookups scoped to the Meta root, not document.
